#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:6
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:8
msgid "`nix registry` - manage the flake registry"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:10
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr "概要"

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:12
msgid "`nix registry` \\[_option_...\\] _subcommand_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:14
msgid "where _subcommand_ is one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:16
msgid ""
"[`nix registry add`](./nix3-registry-add.md) - add/replace flake in user "
"flake registry"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:17
msgid ""
"[`nix registry list`](./nix3-registry-list.md) - list available Nix flakes"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:18
msgid ""
"[`nix registry pin`](./nix3-registry-pin.md) - pin a flake to its current "
"version or to the current version of a flake URL"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:19
msgid ""
"[`nix registry remove`](./nix3-registry-remove.md) - remove flake from user "
"flake registry"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:20
msgid ""
"[`nix registry resolve`](./nix3-registry-resolve.md) - resolve flake "
"references using the registry"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:22
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:24
msgid ""
"`nix registry` provides subcommands for managing _flake registries_. Flake "
"registries are a convenience feature that allows you to refer to flakes "
"using symbolic identifiers such as `nixpkgs`, rather than full URLs such as "
"`git://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs`. You can use these identifiers on the "
"command line (e.g. when you do `nix run nixpkgs#hello`) or in flake input "
"specifications in `flake.nix` files. The latter are automatically resolved "
"to full URLs and recorded in the flake's `flake.lock` file."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:33
msgid ""
"In addition, the flake registry allows you to redirect arbitrary flake "
"references (e.g. `github:NixOS/patchelf`) to another location, such as a "
"local fork."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:37
msgid ""
"There are multiple registries. These are, in order from lowest to highest "
"precedence:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:40
msgid ""
"The global registry, which is a file downloaded from the URL specified by "
"the setting `flake-registry`. It is cached locally and updated automatically "
"when it's older than `tarball-ttl` seconds. The default global registry is "
"kept in [a GitHub repository](https://github.com/NixOS/flake-registry)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:46
msgid ""
"The system registry, which is shared by all users. The default location is `/"
"etc/nix/registry.json`. On NixOS, the system registry can be specified using "
"the NixOS option `nix.registry`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:50
msgid ""
"The user registry `~/.config/nix/registry.json`. This registry can be "
"modified by commands such as `nix registry pin`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:53
msgid ""
"Overrides specified on the command line using the option `--override-flake`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:56
msgid ""
"Note that the system and user registries are not used to resolve flake "
"references in `flake.nix`. They are only used to resolve flake references on "
"the command line."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:58
msgid "Registry format"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:60
msgid "A registry is a JSON file with the following format:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:64
msgid "\"version\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:65
msgid "\"flakes\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:67
msgid "\"from\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:68
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:72
msgid "\"type\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:68
msgid "\"indirect\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:69
msgid "\"id\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:69
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:74
msgid "\"nixpkgs\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:71
msgid "\"to\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:72
msgid "\"github\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:73
msgid "\"owner\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:73
msgid "\"NixOS\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:74
msgid "\"repo\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:82
msgid ""
"That is, it contains a list of objects with attributes `from` and `to`, both "
"of which contain a flake reference in attribute representation. (For "
"example, `{\"type\": \"indirect\", \"id\": \"nixpkgs\"}` is the attribute "
"representation of `nixpkgs`, while `{\"type\": \"github\", \"owner\": "
"\"NixOS\", \"repo\": \"nixpkgs\"}` is the attribute representation of "
"`github:NixOS/nixpkgs`.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:89
msgid ""
"Given some flake reference _R_, a registry entry is used if its `from` flake "
"reference _matches_ _R_. _R_ is then replaced by the _unification_ of the "
"`to` flake reference with _R_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:93
msgid "Matching"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:95
msgid ""
"The `from` flake reference in a registry entry _matches_ some flake "
"reference _R_ if the attributes in `from` are the same as the attributes in "
"`R`. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:99
msgid "`nixpkgs` matches with `nixpkgs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:101
msgid "`nixpkgs` matches with `nixpkgs/nixos-20.09`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:103
msgid "`nixpkgs/nixos-20.09` does not match with `nixpkgs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:105
msgid "`nixpkgs` does not match with `git://github.com/NixOS/patchelf`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:107
msgid "Unification"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:109
msgid ""
"The `to` flake reference in a registry entry is _unified_ with some flake "
"reference _R_ by taking `to` and applying the `rev` and `ref` attributes "
"from _R_, if specified. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:113
msgid ""
"`github:NixOS/nixpkgs` unified with `nixpkgs` produces `github:NixOS/"
"nixpkgs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:115
msgid ""
"`github:NixOS/nixpkgs` unified with `nixpkgs/nixos-20.09` produces `github:"
"NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-20.09`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-registry.md:117
msgid ""
"`github:NixOS/nixpkgs/master` unified with `nixpkgs/nixos-20.09` produces "
"`github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-20.09`."
msgstr ""

